EMBER-01A issue-by-issue reconciliation disposition: COMPLETED.

The exact defect was fixed and merged in PR #454, merge commit 3a683ce6208c6745617eb57d46a44d0b6580c971. Its immutable verification record contains:
- pre-fix --selftest and --dry-run TypeError reproductions;
- post-fix full --selftest exit 0 with P5_AUDIT_SELFTEST_PASS;
- post-fix full --dry-run exit 0 with P5_AUDIT_DRYRUN_DONE;
- receipt spot-checks preserving the expected rho_rank/rho_grow value and na_reason schema.

Public master ca500aabe0f597ab85e762ceb53748724fb0ae98 retains tuple unpacking at the selftest, dry-run, and live call sites. No implementation remainder from #450 is present.

This closure makes no model, capability, benchmark, or research claim.

EMBER-01A issue-by-issue reconciliation disposition: COMPLETED.

The endpoint-precedence defect was fixed and merged in PR #614, merge commit d10de3fef44f145c70e6e99f441028e8e4bcc4ed. Its immutable verification record includes:
- process-entry targeted RED: 4 failing regression cases on pre-fix behavior;
- process-entry GREEN: 83 pass, 0 fail;
- session-init RED for the missing null-preserving resolver and GREEN: 17 pass, 0 fail;
- an end-to-end case proving EMBER_GPU_FREE=1 alone wins when EMBER_MODEL_URL is unset and a persisted endpoint exists;
- explicit disclosure of the unrelated pre-existing full-suite timeout and typecheck defect.

Public master ca500aabe0f597ab85e762ceb53748724fb0ae98 retains the dedicated gpu-free resolution source, the operator-visible source banner, null-preserving session-init resolution, and the regression cases. No implementation remainder from #602 is present.

This closure makes no model, capability, benchmark, or research claim.

Closing as completed after independent verification against current public master fe4d9e2beb5a82573f3f59a5cb05fe9b2c1a097c.

PR #646 (2d4bfc9ecdf2df2c77dac884d1b42ee8d702228e) is an ancestor of current master. The governing c5c_readout.py remains byte-identical to the merged cure, and a fresh replay passed with C5C_READOUT_SELFTEST_PASS.

The frozen prelaunch grammar now enforces the issue's exact bar:

- two rungs remain directional-only;
- W uses a joint-bootstrap confidence interval;
- three rungs are required for uncertainty-aware monotone widening;
- F1, F2, and F3 remain untouched.

No real governed run is being credited here. This issue requested the readout grammar and apparatus before launch; that mechanism is complete, while actual experimental evidence remains a separate open obligation.

EMBER-01A issue-by-issue reconciliation disposition: COMPLETED.

The emitter-side cure and the blocked board-receipt landing were completed in merged PR #647, merge commit 7702907a6a7537b14f647a86308fcbb7ba2dd1ca. Its immutable record contains:
- an exact RED reproduction against pre-fix code using repo-guard PATHPAT;
- GREEN after the fix;
- 84 pre-existing totality tests plus the new regression: 85 passed;
- staged and tree-wide repo-guard PASS;
- an unmodified landed board receipt with zero local-path matches;
- a full receipt-emission surface sweep with explicit residual disclosure.

Merged follow-up PR #660, merge commit 0351594b1f02ad02a4da46c95bd08b6e09396fe2, landed the post-cure board/process visibility receipts.

Public master ca500aabe0f597ab85e762ceb53748724fb0ae98 retains the two sanitizer passes, probe-level token/hash defenses, the regression test, and both receipt generations. A current direct scan of scripts/ember_totality/receipts-totality/ember-totality-20260710T054013Z.json found zero drive, Users, home, or mount-root path matches. No #639 implementation or landing remainder remains.

This closure makes no model, capability, benchmark, or research claim.

